.TH LUMINET 1 "September 2026" "eventhorizon 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
luminet \- simulate and draw Schwarzschild black holes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luminet
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B luminet
renders black holes with thin accretion disks after Luminet (1979), and keeps
a notebook of runs so settings can be compared and revisited. With no
arguments it opens a prompt-based menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B render
Render a single black hole.
.TP
.B sweep
Render a range of one setting side by side.
.TP
.B explain
Describe what each setting is and changes.
.TP
.B log show vary note
List, redraw, vary and annotate recorded runs.
.TP
.B term
Draw a black hole in the terminal.
.TP
.B spin
The live widget; the same as
.BR eventhorizon (1).
.TP
.B animate
Write a looping animation.
.PP
Run
.B luminet
.I command
.B \-\-help
for each command's options.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eventhorizon (1)
